# Order Get It Right -- .gitignore
#
# These are runtime artefacts, never source.  They get regenerated
# automatically on first import (or first test run), so it is safe
# for them to be absent from version control.
#
# Closes OPEN_ITEMS A6.  The .pyc cache at
# 02_Technical/src/server/__pycache__/app.cpython-314.pyc that
# prompted the open item is one of the files covered here; with
# this .gitignore in place, no future operator will see it in the
# tree and waste time wondering whether the bytecode is correct.

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Pytest
.pytest_cache/
.pytest_cache

# Hermes scratch / tmp files (created by agents during sessions; never source)
.hermes-tmp*
*.hermes-tmp

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Backup files (per F2 cleanup seal 2026-07-18)
.bak-pre-*
*.bak-pre-*

# Generated artefacts that are noisy in Git diffs but NOT part of the
# trust anchor. The chain itself (03_Vault/facts_registry.json) and
# the human-readable changelog (04_Validation/changelog.log) are
# deliberately KEPT in source control -- they are the trust anchor,
# and a Git diff of a chain block IS a tamper-evident witness of the
# state at that commit. Excluding them from Git would defeat the
# purpose of adopting Git in parallel.
#
# The four exclusions below are build-output noise that the chain and
# changelog do not depend on:
#   - 03_Vault/affidavit_transcript.txt: regenerated by /api/affidavit
#   - 04_Validation/logs/: runtime logs
#   - 04_Validation/reports/: per-audit Markdown/PDF/DOCX output
#   - 04_Validation/squeal-reports/: per-deception Squeal JSON files
#   - data/outbox/: per-batch audit output
# Each can be re-derived from the chain on demand. The chain is the
# source of truth, not these rendered artefacts.
03_Vault/affidavit_transcript.txt
04_Validation/logs/
04_Validation/reports/
04_Validation/squeal-reports/
data/outbox/
